      "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/d/97f17d/{size}.png",
      "created_at": "2014-12-11T12:05:14.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>This came up in a battle vs Akash'Bhuta, but can apply in various other situations. &nbsp;Mountainous Carapace grants -1 damage dealt to AB and will cause her to deal X damage to herself when destroyed. &nbsp;Do we apply the debuff to this damage? &nbsp;I argue that if the card is destroyed then the protection clause can no longer take effect and she would take X damage. &nbsp;Another player is stating that there is a ruling that she would actually take X-1 damage. &nbsp;It seems to me that if the card is destroyed then any benefits granted by the card would no longer be in effect. &nbsp;Granted, we are applying the \"damage herself\" text so clearly the card still \"exists\" even though it is destroyed, and if one set of text exists to be applied it all must.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>I think I've just about talked myself into agreeing with him, but I'm still interested what the PTB say.&nbsp;</p>",
