      "raw": "<p>This came up in a battle vs Akash&#39;Bhuta, but can apply in various other situations. &nbsp;Mountainous Carapace grants -1 damage dealt to AB and will cause her to deal X damage to herself when destroyed. &nbsp;Do we apply the debuff to this damage? &nbsp;I argue that if the card is destroyed then the protection clause can no longer take effect and she would take X damage. &nbsp;Another player is stating that there is a ruling that she would actually take X-1 damage. &nbsp;It seems to me that if the card is destroyed then any benefits granted by the card would no longer be in effect. &nbsp;Granted, we are applying the &quot;damage herself&quot; text so clearly the card still &quot;exists&quot; even though it is destroyed, and if one set of text exists to be applied it all must.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>I think I&#39;ve just about talked myself into agreeing with him, but I&#39;m still interested what the PTB say.&nbsp;</p>",
